1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,010
Bitter cold, almost dark:
the last evening of the year.

2
00:00:06,133 --> 00:00:09,823
A poor girl shuffled along
in her mother's big slippers.

3
00:00:10,758 --> 00:00:14,968
Carriages raced by; she lost
them, and went on barefoot.

4
00:00:15,675 --> 00:00:18,465
Matches… who will buy my matches?

5
00:00:19,003 --> 00:00:21,113
No one had bought a single match.

6
00:00:21,967 --> 00:00:26,217
Candles gleamed in the windows;
it smelled of roast goose.

7
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:31,230
She huddled in a corner,
afraid to go home to her father.

8
00:00:32,383 --> 00:00:36,613
Her hands were numb.
If she dared strike just one…

9
00:00:38,342 --> 00:00:43,792
How it blazed! A warm iron stove
seemed to stand before her.

10
00:00:44,131 --> 00:00:45,561
Then it went out.

11
00:00:46,633 --> 00:00:52,943
A second: the wall became a veil,
and inside, a roast goose steamed.

12
00:00:53,633 --> 00:00:57,283
It hopped down and waddled
toward her — then darkness.

13
00:00:58,508 --> 00:01:03,458
A third: she sat beneath a
Christmas tree ablaze with candles.

14
00:01:04,300 --> 00:01:09,930
Out it went. The lights rose
and became stars. One fell.

15
00:01:10,324 --> 00:01:11,534
Someone is dying.

16
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:15,370
Her grandmother,
the only one who had loved her,

17
00:01:15,460 --> 00:01:19,770
had said: a falling star
is a soul going to God.

18
00:01:20,467 --> 00:01:25,177
A fourth — and there stood
Grandmother, shining and kind.

19
00:01:25,925 --> 00:01:28,495
Grandmother! Take me with you!

20
00:01:30,175 --> 00:01:33,665
She struck the whole bundle,
to keep her near.

21
00:01:34,550 --> 00:01:37,790
Grandmother took her in
her arms, and they flew up,

22
00:01:37,830 --> 00:01:41,880
where there is no cold,
no hunger, no fear.

23
00:01:42,592 --> 00:01:49,202
At dawn she sat there still,
rosy-cheeked and smiling — frozen to death.

24
00:01:49,758 --> 00:01:51,348
She wanted to warm herself.

25
00:01:53,758 --> 00:01:58,628
No one knew the beautiful things she
had seen, or the joy she had gone to.

